The FCN, ShortChunkCNN, ShortChunkCNN_Res, Musicnn and CRNN architectures in
`model_zoo.py`, and the convolutional blocks in `modules.py`, are ported from
that repository and adapted for hierarchical era classification (four softmax
heads over decade / half-decade / quarter-decade / year, plus a hierarchical
consistency loss). The original architectures are described in:

  Won et al., "Evaluation of CNN-based automatic music tagging models",
  SMC 2020.
  Choi et al., "Automatic tagging using deep convolutional neural networks",
  ISMIR 2016.
  Choi et al., "Convolutional recurrent neural networks for music
  classification", ICASSP 2017.
  Pons et al., "End-to-end learning for music audio tagging at scale",
  ISMIR 2017.

Billboard Hot 100 chart entries in `csv/` are derived from the Billboard Hot
100 chart data compiled at https://github.com/utdata/rwd-billboard-data.
Melon chart entries are derived from the Melon year-end and weekly charts.
Neither this repository nor its releases distribute any audio recordings.
